{
  "id": "outcome-dependence",
  "term": "outcome dependence",
  "definition": "Outcome dependence is the degree to which a person relies on a powerful authority for desired social or material results because that authority controls valued resources. In social psychology, it reflects how much someone depends on the system represented by that authority.",
